WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.240
I ran across this cool shawl,

and I love the simplicity of the lace.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.360
And I immediately thought,

"we can knit this on the machine."

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.840
Yes, the original is in garter stitch.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.000
There are no purl stitches,

hence the name.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.000
But by knitting it on the machine,

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.240
we can have the best of both worlds

with different texture on both sides.

7
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.040
But bells started going off in my head

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.960
about biasing when transferring eyelets

in the same direction every time.

9
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:37.440
Here's the stitch pattern. Create an eyelet,

every other needle, every other row.

10
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.400
I started to work the transfers
manually
on my mid-gauge machine.

11
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.600
Starting on the left,
I transferred, knit
across then knit a row.

12
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:53.480
Then transferred again knit across, knit a row.

But those little bells were right.

13
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.240
I could quickly see that by transferring

14
00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.280
in the same direction every

time, the knitting was biasing.

15
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:06.360
Even though technically it's biasing,

the stitch pattern is really pretty

16
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.800
and could be a beautiful scarf

or cowl with a diagonal design.

17
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.080
An automatic patterning machine would

make really quick work of this.

18
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.720
But to prevent the bias,

I alternated the transfers.

19
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.080
Starting by working left to right,

20
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.600
I transferred my eyelets

to every other needle.

21
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.120
Knit across and knit back.

22
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:44.040
Then I transferred in the other

direction from right to left.

23
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.320
This straightened out the knitting

and makes a simple, beautiful,

24
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.760
open work lace that we could

use for this Purl Thief Shawl.

25
00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:59.600
By the way, if you don't like triangular

shawls, borrow the ideas from this design

26
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.600
and use the Knit it Now

tool and make it a rectangle.

27
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.000
You're the designer.

